// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: a value of type `R` may not be a reference
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: A `type` alias is not a way past that rule
//
// DF-188b, audit row R50: the back-conversion is what INHABITS an alias, so it
// is the third position the alias bypass needed. `R(&x)` builds a value of a
// type that IS `&Int` and hands it to a binding, where a bare `&x` has been
// refused since DF-163d — the alias was the only thing hiding it. Refusing the
// construction is what makes the field and generic-argument refusals total:
// there is no longer any way to produce the value they decline to store.

type R = &Int

func main() {
    var x = 7
    let r = R(&x)
    print("made one")
}
